/code> to a <code>utc_time</code> representing the same point in time.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A <span class=\"t-lc\">std::chrono::utc_time</span> representing the same point in time as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t</span></code>, computed as if by constructing a value of the return type from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t.<span class=\"me1\">time_since_epoch</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and subtracting <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">378691210s</span></code> (378691210 is the number of seconds between the epochs of the two clocks: 1958-01-01 00:00:00 TAI and 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/tai_clock/from_utc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>from_utc</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  converts <code>utc_time</code> to <code>tai_time</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/clock_cast\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clock_cast</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  convert time points of one clock to another <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/tai_clock","title":"std::chrono::tai_clock"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::chrono::tai_